            <body>
                <p>Problem Statement Title	<br>
Extreme Heatwave Early Warning and Human Thermal Stress Index<br>
Description	<br>
In recent years, the frequency, duration, and intensity of heatwaves across India have escalated sharply due to climate change. However, traditional meteorological warnings rely almost exclusively on ambient dry-bulb temperature thresholds. This creates a critical vulnerability:standard forecasts ignore the deadly compounding effects of relative humidity, wind speed, and solar radiation on the human body.</p><p></p><p>A temperature of 40Â°C at 20% humidity feels vastly different from 40Â°C at 70% humidityâ€”the latter can be fatal. Current public health infrastructure lacks localized, impact-based forecasting that translates raw weather data into actual physiological risk, human thermal stress levels, and projected mortality rates.</p><p></p><p>The challenge is to design an intelligent, localized early warning system that shifts heatwave forecasting from 'what the weather will be' to 'what the weather will do' to human health.</p><p></p><p>Participants need to build a predictive platform that computes a comprehensive Human Thermal Stress Index (integrating temperature, humidity, wind, and radiation) and links it directly to an automated Mortality Risk Index. The system should offer high-resolution forecasts to help municipal corporations, healthcare systems, and disaster management authorities deploy targeted,preemptive interventions.</p><p></p><p>Develop algorithms to calculate advanced heat stress metrics such as the Wet-Bulb Globe Temperature (WBGT), Universal Thermal Climate Index (UTCI), or Heat Index (HI) rather than relying on temperature alone. Integrate historical public health, demographic (e.g., elderly or outdoor worker density), and localized weather data to predict heat-induced mortality and hospitalization spikes 3 to 5 days in advance. A dynamic GIS-mapped dashboard providing colorcoded, hyper-local alerts (Zone/Ward level) paired with actionable, automated public health advisories. An API capable of pushing automated SMS/WhatsApp regional alerts or localized triggers for city administration to initiate heat action plans (e.g., opening cooling centers, adjusting power grids, shifting outdoor work hours).</p><p></p><p>Proposed Features</p><ol><li><p><strong>Hyper-local ward-level heat risk mapping</strong> — Shows heat risk for individual wards and neighborhoods.</p></li><li><p><strong>Real-time temperature ingestion</strong> — Continuously collects the latest temperature readings.</p></li><li><p><strong>Relative humidity monitoring</strong> — Measures humidity to identify increased thermal stress.</p></li><li><p><strong>Wind speed and direction integration</strong> — Evaluates how wind affects body cooling.</p></li><li><p><strong>Solar radiation measurement</strong> — Accounts for direct and reflected heat exposure.</p></li><li><p><strong>WBGT calculation</strong> — Calculates Wet-Bulb Globe Temperature for occupational heat stress.</p></li><li><p><strong>UTCI calculation</strong> — Estimates physiological stress using multiple weather parameters.</p></li><li><p><strong>Heat Index calculation</strong> — Determines how hot conditions feel to the human body.</p></li><li><p><strong>Human Thermal Stress Index</strong> — Combines weather factors into a unified health-risk score.</p></li><li><p><strong>Automated Mortality Risk Index</strong> — Estimates the probability of heat-related deaths.</p></li><li><p><strong>3–5 day heat mortality prediction</strong> — Forecasts potential mortality spikes several days ahead.</p></li><li><p><strong>Hospitalization spike prediction</strong> — Predicts increases in heat-related hospital admissions.</p></li><li><p><strong>Vulnerable population mapping</strong> — Identifies areas with populations highly sensitive to heat.</p></li><li><p><strong>Elderly population density analysis</strong> — Highlights wards with higher elderly concentrations.</p></li><li><p><strong>Outdoor worker density mapping</strong> — Identifies areas with greater occupational heat exposure.</p></li><li><p><strong>Children and infant vulnerability mapping</strong> — Flags locations with heat-sensitive young populations.</p></li><li><p><strong>Slum and high-density settlement mapping</strong> — Detects communities with greater heat exposure and limited cooling.</p></li><li><p><strong>Historical heatwave mortality analysis</strong> — Uses past deaths to understand heat-related mortality patterns.</p></li><li><p><strong>Historical hospitalization correlation</strong> — Links previous weather conditions with hospital admissions.</p></li><li><p><strong>Ward-wise heat vulnerability score</strong> — Assigns each ward a combined exposure and vulnerability score.</p></li><li><p><strong>AI/ML-based mortality forecasting</strong> — Uses machine learning to predict heat-related health outcomes.</p></li><li><p><strong>Time-series heatwave prediction</strong> — Detects patterns to forecast upcoming heat events.</p></li><li><p><strong>Heatwave severity classification</strong> — Categorizes heatwaves from moderate to extreme.</p></li><li><p><strong>Heatwave duration prediction</strong> — Estimates how long dangerous conditions may persist.</p></li><li><p><strong>Night-time heat stress monitoring</strong> — Detects dangerous overnight temperatures that prevent recovery.</p></li><li><p><strong>Minimum-temperature risk detection</strong> — Identifies health risks caused by unusually high minimum temperatures.</p></li><li><p><strong>Urban heat-island detection</strong> — Finds hotter urban zones caused by buildings and infrastructure.</p></li><li><p><strong>Satellite-based land surface temperature analysis</strong> — Uses satellite imagery to identify spatial heat patterns.</p></li><li><p><strong>Hyper-local weather interpolation</strong> — Generates detailed weather estimates between available stations.</p></li><li><p><strong>GIS-based interactive risk dashboard</strong> — Displays heat and health risks on an interactive map.</p></li><li><p><strong>Color-coded ward-level alerts</strong> — Uses simple colors to communicate different risk levels.</p></li><li><p><strong>Individualized risk scoring</strong> — Estimates heat risk based on location and personal vulnerability factors.</p></li><li><p><strong>Age-specific thermal risk estimation</strong> — Calculates different risk levels for different age groups.</p></li><li><p><strong>Occupational heat-risk assessment</strong> — Estimates heat exposure for outdoor and physically demanding jobs.</p></li><li><p><strong>Automated heat-health advisories</strong> — Generates location-specific recommendations based on current risk.</p></li><li><p><strong>SMS alert integration</strong> — Sends emergency heat warnings directly through SMS.</p></li><li><p><strong>WhatsApp alert integration</strong> — Delivers localized alerts and advisories through WhatsApp.</p></li><li><p><strong>Mobile app notifications</strong> — Pushes real-time heat warnings to registered users.</p></li><li><p><strong>Government API for automated alerts</strong> — Allows authorities to integrate risk alerts into existing systems.</p></li><li><p><strong>Cooling-center recommendation system</strong> — Suggests nearby cooling centers for high-risk populations.</p></li><li><p><strong>Outdoor work-hour optimization</strong> — Recommends safer working hours during extreme heat.</p></li><li><p><strong>Heat-action-plan automation triggers</strong> — Automatically recommends predefined government response actions.</p></li><li><p><strong>Power-grid stress prediction</strong> — Forecasts electricity demand caused by increased cooling requirements.</p></li><li><p><strong>Drinking-water demand prediction</strong> — Estimates additional water requirements during heatwaves.</p></li><li><p><strong>Ambulance and emergency-service demand forecasting</strong> — Predicts increased demand for emergency medical services.</p></li><li><p><strong>Hospital bed and resource allocation alerts</strong> — Helps hospitals prepare staff, beds, and equipment in advance.</p></li><li><p><strong>Real-time sensor/IoT integration</strong> — Collects hyper-local environmental data from connected sensors.</p></li><li><p><strong>Historical and forecast data visualization</strong> — Compares current conditions with past and predicted heat levels.</p></li><li><p><strong>Explainable AI for risk predictions</strong> — Shows why the system assigned a particular risk level.</p></li><li><p><strong>Early-warning escalation and response tracking</strong> — Tracks alerts, authority actions, and response effectiveness.</p></li></ol><p></p><p><br><br></p>
            </body>
            </html>
        